      "message": "fix(motion): hold the crossing law on corner arcs one corner at a time\n\nPR #2273 sent the rounded walks of Waterline and Offset rings through\npost_crossing_free. That law maps a crossing arc onto the vertices of\nthe pass, and a rounded walk has new vertices, so one hit gave the whole\npass back to plain chords: every corner arc was lost (corner_arc_radius\nred on main).\n\n- blend_cross.rs: the law keeps the walks as fitted and rounds them\n  again each round. A corner arc that crosses another feed bans its own\n  corner (kept sharp, counted in the fillet note). A fitted arc that\n  crosses goes back to the chords of the plan. After CROSS_ROUNDS no\n  corner is rounded and the classic law holds.\n- arc_touch.rs: a chord that stays within 1e-5 mm of the tangent at an\n  end of a corner arc, the radius mismatch counted in, is a touch and\n  not a crossing. Only corner arcs get this; Adaptive and the 3D ladder\n  pass no corner arcs and read as before.\n- fillet.rs: fillet_corners_except takes the banned corners and gives\n  the trace of each added or trimmed arc.\n\nDecision: docs/decisions/2317-blend-crossing-law.md\n\nFixes #2317\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
